Question 18: Given x = np.arange(1, 25).reshape(2, 12), split it into 3 equal parts. Split it after the 3rd and 4th columns. Then split np.arange(1, 7) into 4 parts with np.array_split.

AIM: Understanding Array Splitting

Code:
import numpy as np
x=np.arange(1, 25).reshape(2, 12)
split_equal = np.split(x, 3, axis=1)
print("\nSplit into 3 equal parts:")
for part in split_equal:
    print(part)
split_cols = np.split(x, [3, 4], axis=1)
print("\nSplit after 3rd and 4th columns:")
for part in split_cols:
    print(part)
y = np.arange(1, 7)
split_array = np.array_split(y, 4)
print("\nSplit np.arange(1,7) into 4 parts:")
for part in split_array:
    print(part)

Output:
Split into 3 equal parts:
[[ 1  2  3  4]
 [13 14 15 16]]
[[ 5  6  7  8]
 [17 18 19 20]]
[[ 9 10 11 12]
 [21 22 23 24]]

Split after 3rd and 4th columns:
