 [13 14 15]]
[[ 4]
 [16]]
[[ 5  6  7  8  9 10 11 12]
 [17 18 19 20 21 22 23 24]]

Split np.arange(1,7) into 4 parts:
[1 2]
[3 4]
[5]
[6]

Explanation:
Functions used: np.split(), np.array_split()
Usage: np.split(x,3,axis=1) divides the array into 3 equal parts along the column axis.
np.split(x,[3,4],axis=1) splits array after 3rd and 4th column
np.split_array(y,4) splits array into 4 nearly equal parts. Its a more flexible function as it allows arrays where division is not equal as well.
